From 5236e4e0d5f704dc0d3e279d141d78f52d52a833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 15:24:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: OPTIONS-REGISTRY GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK - CORRECTNESS
 FAIL, GEMM returns NaN

The slot is exercisable for the first time, and it does not pass. Two blockers
were retired to get there, then the kernel itself failed.

g64 corpus. llama-quantize on this fork emits canonical type-42 at QK2_0 = 64;
that premise was verified at ggml/src/ggml-common.h:187 and
src/llama-quant.cpp:807 BEFORE being relied on. Built from
qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-fp16.gguf, exit 0. Geometry proven by tensor-span probe
rather than by filename: 168 type-42 tensors, span-classified g64 on all 167
measurable, g128 = 0.

Reachability, previously unknown. make_cpu_buft_list() (src/llama-model.cpp:
902-935) appends the device HOST buffer type before the CPU extra buffer types,
so on a Vulkan build Vulkan_Host/CPU_Mapped always wins and CPU_REPACK is never
selected. --no-host is required to reach the code at all, for any model. Every
earlier byte-identity result in this slot was therefore taken with the repack
path untaken in BOTH arms and proved nothing about these kernels.

Engagement proven, not assumed. ON emits "CPU_REPACK model buffer size" of
4.68 / 84.16 / 95.98 MiB depending on how much of the model is Q2_0; OFF emits
no CPU_REPACK line at all and CPU_Mapped grows by the same amount. Only Q2_0
can occupy that buffer on x86, since the Q8_0/Q5_0 repack arms are NEON-gated.

The defect. On a multi-token prefill, ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0
(ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:6643) returns NaN logits: the server
serialises every logprob as null and the top-3 degenerates to vocabulary ids
0,1,2 in order, the signature of a sort over all-NaN. OFF returns finite, stable
logprobs on the same prompt (top-1 -2.3078582286834717, bit-identical across two
fresh launches). Reproduced across 2 fresh launches x 3 requests per arm,
deterministic in both directions.

GEMV does not produce NaN, but its bit-exactness is UNVERIFIED and is not
claimed either way: a 1-token prompt is not reproducible even with repack OFF,
and -ub 1 - the clean way to force GEMV with a real prompt - crashes this build
in BOTH arms (rc=3221226505), a separate pre-existing defect not attributable
to this branch.

Performance deliberately NOT measured. Step 3 was gated on correctness passing;
it did not. No t/s figure from this slot may be quoted.

NOT merged to master. Default should stay 0 until the GEMM inner loop is fixed.

Ported-mechanism: PrismML x86 AVX512-VNNI repack GEMV/GEMM for Q1_0 and Q2_0 (9fcaed763, 79697f23a)
Source-path: docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/run-journal.jsonl, 110/vnni-g64/, 110/vnni-g64-mixed/
Origin: ArifiLabs/vnni-repack
---
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

