+++ b/docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ safe measurement posture.
 | `EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH` | unset | Loads a generated Q4_0 expert bundle from SSD for supported MoE models. | Use when the model’s experts cannot remain in RAM/VRAM and a compatible bundle exists. | Capability proven: 21B streamed coherently at `5.9–6.1` CPU decode t/s; Qwen3.6-35B streamed from a 17 GB bundle at `1.6` CPU decode t/s; tiered `-ngl 99 -cmoe` reached `3.0` t/s. It is not a claim of sparse Vulkan execution. |
 | `MAX_N_CACHED` | implementation-selected; document the chosen value in a run record | Bounds hot-expert RAM cache capacity. | Increase only after measuring cache pressure, RAM headroom, and bundle I/O behavior. | No independently accepted ON/OFF benchmark is recorded. Treat as a measured tuning variable, not a presumed gain. |
 | `POWERINFER_IOCP` | **ON** when unset (Windows only; any value other than an exact `0` keeps IOCP). `POWERINFER_IOCP=0` selects the pre-M2b synchronous path. | Scope: the Windows expert-bundle read path only (`powerinfer/moe_sparse_pipeline/iou.cpp` + the `io_worker_main` Windows branch); it is inert on Linux, which keeps vendored `io_uring` unconditionally. ON issues bounded IOCP async positioned reads (ring of `io_queue_depth`=512) so storage latency overlaps the token path; OFF issues blocking `ReadFile`+`OVERLAPPED` positioned reads, one at a time. | Flip to `0` to recover from a suspected streaming deadlock, an IOCP assert, or to A/B the read path without a recompile. Only meaningful with `EXPERT_BUNDLE_PATH` set — with no bundle there is no expert IO and the flag does nothing. | **Direction UNRESOLVED — neither a gain nor a regression is established.** Same-binary A/B, 2026-07-24 (llama-server, 21B + bundle-21b, `-ngl 0 -b 8 -ub 8`, 4× n64 ignore_eos, fresh server per arm, env flip only — no HEAD confound): **OFF `3.77 / 3.60 / 5.94 / 3.94`** (mean `4.31`) vs **ON `2.42 / 8.74 / 5.20 / 6.28`** (mean `5.66`). The `+31%` mean gap is **noise, not signal, and must not be quoted**: within-arm spread on ON alone (`2.42→8.74` = `6.32`) exceeds the between-arm gap (`1.35`), and with n=1 per cell the ON mean swings `4.63`–`6.74` depending on which single roll is dropped — straddling the OFF mean. Both arms ran memory-starved (`2.4–4.0 GB` free during), and two confounds favour ON anyway (it ran second with a warmer page cache, and launched with `1.2 GB` more headroom). This is the terminal verdict at this RAM; a real measurement needs sustained headroom and repeated rolls per cell. Sol's `10–40%` cold-regime figure is an audit *estimate*, never measured here (`RESULTS-sparse-runs-on-windows.md:286`; codex job `task-mrwgwtze-hw1o8t.log`) — do not cite it as a result. Correctness ON is proven: streaming engaged (working set `4.77 GB` vs an `11.4 GB` model file, identical in both arms), coherent output, zero IOCP errors, clean shutdown. Ring-full (`n_inflight ≥ 512`) and `ERROR_IO_PENDING` branches remain **unexercised**. |
-| `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK` | **ON** when unset (any value other than an exact `0` keeps it). `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=0` restores the exact pre-slot behaviour on every architecture. | Scope: the CPU repack *type-selection* for `GGML_TYPE_Q1_0` and `GGML_TYPE_Q2_0` only, inside `ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type()` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp`). ON lets those two types claim the `CPU_REPACK` buffer type and use the interleaved 4×8 GEMV/GEMM kernels (AVX512-VNNI on x86, NEON+DP on Arm); OFF returns `nullptr` for both, so batched `mul_mat` falls back to per-row `vec_dot`. It does **not** touch Q4_0/Q4_K/Q8_0 repack, and it is inert on any model containing no Q1_0/Q2_0 tensors. **NOT covered by this toggle:** the x86 Q2_0 `vec_dot` fast path added alongside it — that is selected at compile time by `__AVX512VNNI__`/`__AVXVNNI__` exactly like every other arch kernel in the tree, and is bit-exact with the scalar loop it replaces, so it is an implementation, not an option. | Flip to `0` to fall back without a recompile if the repack kernels are ever suspected in a wrong-output or crash report, or to A/B the repack mechanism in isolation. Only meaningful for a **g64** Q1_0/Q2_0 model — see the cost cell. | **Cost ON: UNMEASURED. Cost OFF: UNMEASURED. Correctness on real weights: UNVERIFIED.** All three are blocked on a missing artifact, not on effort: **every ternary GGUF on this box is g128 payload** (34 B / 128 values), verified by tensor-span geometry across all 7 files in `models/hf/prism-ml/` and `models/gguf/ternary/` — `g64_tensors=0` in every one. These kernels are g64-only by construction (`QK2_0 == 64`, `block_q2_0x4 == block<2,4>`), and `PHASE2c-g128-type-architecture.md:175` forbids retargeting them to g128 without separate equivalence testing. So **no locally-held model can reach this code at all**, in either arm. What was verified, 2026-07-24 (llama-server, `Ternary-Bonsai-8B-Q2_0.g128.gguf` native type-43, `-ngl 0 -c 512 -t 8`, 48 tokens, temp 0, seed 42, fresh server per arm, env flip only): the g128 path is **unregressed and the g64 guard holds** — ON and OFF produced **byte-identical** output (md5 `ac5df68c…`), coherent, `1.44` vs `1.45` t/s decode (a `1%` gap that is noise and must not be quoted as a result — the repack path is untaken in both arms, so identity is the expected outcome and the *only* claim made). To retire the UNMEASURED cells, obtain a genuine g64 Q2_0 or Q1_0 GGUF — smallest acceptable source: a Bonsai-8B re-export at `QK2_0 = 64` (≈2 GB), which fits this box with headroom. |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK` | **ON** when unset (any value other than an exact `0` keeps it). `GGML_ARIFI_VNNI_REPACK=0` restores the exact pre-slot behaviour on every architecture. | Scope: the CPU repack *type-selection* for `GGML_TYPE_Q1_0` and `GGML_TYPE_Q2_0` only, inside `ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type()` (`ggml/src/ggml-cpu/repack.cpp`). ON lets those two types claim the `CPU_REPACK` buffer type and use the interleaved 4×8 GEMV/GEMM kernels (AVX512-VNNI on x86, NEON+DP on Arm); OFF returns `nullptr` for both, so batched `mul_mat` falls back to per-row `vec_dot`. It does **not** touch Q4_0/Q4_K/Q8_0 repack, and it is inert on any model containing no Q1_0/Q2_0 tensors. **NOT covered by this toggle:** the x86 Q2_0 `vec_dot` fast path added alongside it — that is selected at compile time by `__AVX512VNNI__`/`__AVXVNNI__` exactly like every other arch kernel in the tree, and is bit-exact with the scalar loop it replaces, so it is an implementation, not an option. | **Keep at `0` on this fork until the GEMM defect in the cost cell is fixed.** The unset default (ON) is PrismML's and is not safe here. Only reachable at all for a **g64** Q1_0/Q2_0 model, and on a Vulkan-enabled build only with `--no-host` - see the cost cell. | **CORRECTNESS FAILS: the x86 AVX512-VNNI Q2_0 GEMM produces NaN. Do not merge; do not ship ON. Performance deliberately NOT measured** - the correctness gate failed, so a speed number would be meaningless.<br><br>**Both prior blockers are retired.** (1) *A g64 corpus now exists.* `llama-quantize <src> <dst> Q2_0` on this fork emits canonical type-42 at `QK2_0 = 64` (`ggml/src/ggml-common.h:187`; `LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q2_0 -> GGML_TYPE_Q2_0` at `src/llama-quant.cpp:807`). Built 2026-07-24 from `research/local-inference/models/gguf/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-fp16.gguf`, exit 0. Geometry proven by tensor-span probe rather than filename: `qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct-Q2_0-g64.gguf` carries 168 type-42 tensors, span-classified **g64 on all 167 measurable, g128 = 0**. (2) *Reaching the code needs `--no-host`.* `make_cpu_buft_list()` (`src/llama-model.cpp:902-935`) appends the device **host** buffer type BEFORE the CPU extra buffer types, so on a Vulkan build `Vulkan_Host`/`CPU_Mapped` always wins and `CPU_REPACK` is never selected - the path is unreachable by default **regardless of model**. This is why the earlier g128 byte-identity result proved nothing about these kernels.<br><br>**Engagement is proven, not assumed.** ON emits `load_tensors: CPU_REPACK model buffer size = 95.98 MiB` (all-Q2_0 model), `84.16 MiB` (Q8_0 base + Q2_0 FFN) or `4.68 MiB` (Q8_0 base + 4x `ffn_down`); OFF emits **no `CPU_REPACK` line at all** and `CPU_Mapped` grows by the same amount. Only Q2_0 can occupy that buffer on x86 here, since the Q8_0/Q5_0 repack arms are NEON-gated.<br><br>**The defect** (llama-server, `qwen2.5-0.5b-light-q8_0-4xffndownQ2_0-g64.gguf`, `-ngl 0 -c 512 -t 8 --no-host`, temp 0, top_k 1, seed 42, `cache_prompt` false, fresh server per arm, env flip only): on a **multi-token prefill** (10 tokens, so `ggml_gemm_q2_0_4x8_q8_0`, `ggml/src/ggml-cpu/arch/x86/repack.cpp:6643`) the ON arm returns **NaN logits** - the server serialises every `logprob` as `null` and the top-3 degenerates to vocabulary ids 0,1,2 in order, the signature of a sort over all-NaN; output is `!!!!`. The OFF arm on the same prompt returns finite, stable logprobs (top-1 `-2.3078582286834717`, bit-identical across two fresh launches). Reproduced across **2 launches x 3 requests per arm, deterministic in both directions**.<br><br>**Not NaN, but not cleared either.** With a 1-token prefill (`ggml_gemv_q2_0_4x8_q8_0`, same file:6586) the ON arm returns finite logprobs, so GEMV does not produce NaN. Its **bit-exactness is UNVERIFIED**: a 1-token prompt is not reproducible even with repack OFF (top-1 differed run-to-run at `-3.607` vs `-3.223`), so it cannot adjudicate; and `-ub 1`, the clean way to force GEMV with a real prompt, **crashes this build in both arms** (`rc=3221226505`, STATUS_STACK_BUFFER_OVERRUN) - a separate pre-existing defect, not attributable to this branch. PrismML's bit-exactness claim is therefore **falsified for GEMM and untested for GEMV** on this hardware.<br><br>**Audit for the Sol round:** `repack_q2_0_to_q2_0_4_bl()` and `make_block_q2_0x4()` (`repack.cpp:4053`, `:3231`) were read and are size-consistent (src 18 B/block x 4 rows -> dst 72 B, full 64-byte `qs` written and fully consumed), and the GEMV block/activation stride handling is correct (`QK2_0/QK8_0 = 2` activation blocks per weight block, `:6613-6614`). The audit therefore points at the **GEMM inner loop**, not the repack layout. Superseded claim for the record: **UNMEASURED** All three are blocked on a missing artifact, not on effort: **every ternary GGUF on this box is g128 payload** (34 B / 128 values), verified by tensor-span geometry across all 7 files in `models/hf/prism-ml/` and `models/gguf/ternary/` — `g64_tensors=0` in every one. These kernels are g64-only by construction (`QK2_0 == 64`, `block_q2_0x4 == block<2,4>`), and `PHASE2c-g128-type-architecture.md:175` forbids retargeting them to g128 without separate equivalence testing. So **no locally-held model can reach this code at all**, in either arm. What was verified, 2026-07-24 (llama-server, `Ternary-Bonsai-8B-Q2_0.g128.gguf` native type-43, `-ngl 0 -c 512 -t 8`, 48 tokens, temp 0, seed 42, fresh server per arm, env flip only): the g128 path is **unregressed and the g64 guard holds** — ON and OFF produced **byte-identical** output (md5 `ac5df68c…`), coherent, `1.44` vs `1.45` t/s decode (a `1%` gap that is noise and must not be quoted as a result — the repack path is untaken in both arms, so identity is the expected outcome and the *only* claim made). To retire the UNMEASURED cells, obtain a genuine g64 Q2_0 or Q1_0 GGUF — smallest acceptable source: a Bonsai-8B re-export at `QK2_0 = 64` (≈2 GB), which fits this box with headroom. |
 | `LANE110_PROF=1` | unset | Emits per-operation timing for pipeline initialization, scheduling, build tasks, and forward execution. | Diagnosis only. Disable for benchmark runs. | Pipeline-init reuse itself reduced rebuild work from `2472 µs` to `0–2 µs`; profiler overhead has not been independently quantified. |
 | `LANE110_PREFETCH_CAP` | implementation default, currently `3*n_expert_used` | Limits standalone expert prefetch aggressiveness. | Sweep under cache pressure after establishing the baseline. | Recorded server sequences: default approximately `[5.07/9.03/9.58/12.01]`; cap `1` `[5.13/9.88/10.29/11.22]`; cap `96` `[5.79/11.73/12.19/11.26]`. Default retained because apparent ramp differences require controlled retest. |
 | `--ctx-checkpoints 0` | `0` | Disables server prompt rewind/checkpoints. | Keep off unless a workload demonstrably requires rewind semantics. | Largest historical gain: stock rewind `39.9/68.4/280`; ON_DEVICE checkpoint `84.8/128.8/341.6`; disabled approximately `101/150/372` across short/medium/long prefill. |
